WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.829
Heidi filled her pockets with the two furry bundles, one for herself and one for Clara.

2
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:12.015
The priest said he would deliver the rest of the kittens to Clara the following day.

3
00:00:12.016 --> 00:00:15.117
The boy with the organ led Heidi home.

4
00:00:15.118 --> 00:00:21.850
When they arrived, Sebastian pulled Heidi inside and slammed the door without noticing the little boy.

5
00:00:21.851 --> 00:00:24.908
"Hurry, miss! They are waiting for you at the dining room table.

6
00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:28.893
Fraulein looks like a loaded cannon ready to explode!"

7
00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:34.986
When Heidi stepped into the dining room, Fraulein did not look up and Clara didn’t speak.

8
00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:38.624
Once Heidi was seated, Fraulein said icily,

9
00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:41.582
"I will punish you after dinner, Heidi.

10
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:45.770
It was rude and wicked for you to leave the house without permission."

11
00:00:45.771 --> 00:00:48.589
"Meow!" came the answer back.

12
00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.680
Fraulein trembled with anger.

13
00:00:50.681 --> 00:00:54.377
"How dare you answer me as if it were a joke?!"

14
00:00:54.378 --> 00:00:56.929
"I didn’t . . . ," began Heidi.

15
00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.979
"Meow, meow!" she was interrupted.

16
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.734
Sebastian’s face broke into a smile.

17
00:01:03.735 --> 00:01:09.299
He had figured out what was going on and had to cover his mouth to keep from bursting into laughter.

18
00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.191
Clara looked at Heidi in alarm.

19
00:01:11.192 --> 00:01:12.798
"It’s the kittens!"

20
00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:15.909
said Heidi, and the kittens meowed again.

21
00:01:15.910 --> 00:01:20.256
"What?! Kittens!" shrieked Fraulein.

22
00:01:20.257 --> 00:01:24.846
"Sebastian! Find the horrible things and take them away!"

23
00:01:24.847 --> 00:01:28.246
She leapt from the table and ran into the study.

24
00:01:28.247 --> 00:01:31.850
"You must help us," said Clara to Sebastian.

25
00:01:31.851 --> 00:01:35.286
"The kittens need a home," said Heidi.

26
00:01:35.287 --> 00:01:38.985
"I will see to it," answered Sebastian willingly.

27
00:01:38.986 --> 00:01:45.311
He found a warm basket and put the two kittens in a safe place where Fraulein was not likely to go.

28
00:01:45.312 --> 00:01:50.880
The next morning, Sebastian had just shown the tutor into the study when he heard the doorbell.

29
00:01:50.881 --> 00:01:56.568
He opened the door, and there in front of him was a messy little boy carrying a hand organ.

30
00:01:56.569 --> 00:01:59.447
"I want to see Clara," said the boy.

31
00:01:59.448 --> 00:02:01.437
"She owes me four pennies."

32
00:02:01.438 --> 00:02:03.586
"What for?" asked Sebastian.

33
00:02:03.587 --> 00:02:06.377
"For walking Heidi to the church and then home."

34
00:02:06.378 --> 00:02:10.470
"Oh," thought Sebastian, "this is more of Miss Heidi’s mischief."

35
00:02:10.471 --> 00:02:14.251
He brought the boy into the house and showed him the study.

36
00:02:14.252 --> 00:02:16.864
"Clara is inside," he said.

37
00:02:16.865 --> 00:02:19.389
"Be sure to play your organ the moment you enter.

38
00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:21.146
Clara loves music."

39
00:02:21.147 --> 00:02:25.281
Fraulein, of course, ran to the study as soon as she heard the organ.

40
00:02:25.282 --> 00:02:30.085
Inside, the messy little boy was playing noisily and with great energy.

41
00:02:30.086 --> 00:02:33.971
Clara was delighted and Heidi clapped her hands.

42
00:02:33.972 --> 00:02:39.012
"Stop it! Stop it at once!" screamed Fraulein Rottenmeier.

43
00:02:39.013 --> 00:02:41.049
"Take him out, Sebastian.

44
00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:42.916
Take him out right now!"

45
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:45.182
Sebastian pulled the boy out of the room.

46
00:02:45.183 --> 00:02:48.515
At the front door, he kindly gave the boy his money.

47
00:02:48.516 --> 00:02:54.431
"Here are four pennies from Miss Clara and three more for the music," said Sebastian.

48
00:02:54.432 --> 00:02:58.206
Fraulein decided to stay and watch the rest of the lesson.

49
00:02:58.207 --> 00:03:01.732
Soon, Heidi and Clara had settled down to their work again.

50
00:03:01.733 --> 00:03:06.369
There was a knock on the study door, and Sebastian entered with a large basket.

51
00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.359
"This was just delivered for you, miss," he said to Clara.

52
00:03:10.360 --> 00:03:13.580
"For me?" said Clara.

53
00:03:13.581 --> 00:03:19.541
"I think the girls should finish their lesson before the basket is opened," said Fraulein.

54
00:03:19.542 --> 00:03:23.404
Sebastian placed the basket on the floor and shut the door.

55
00:03:23.405 --> 00:03:30.667
The lesson continued quietly, and then, all of a sudden, Fraulein sprang up and jumped onto her chair.

56
00:03:30.668 --> 00:03:34.317
There were kittens scampering all over the floor.

57
00:03:34.318 --> 00:03:36.151
Clara was thrilled.

58
00:03:36.152 --> 00:03:39.204
"Oh, the dear little things!

59
00:03:39.205 --> 00:03:42.325
Look, Heidi! How pretty they are!"

60
00:03:42.326 --> 00:03:46.262
Fraulein was so overcome with horror that she couldn’t speak.

61
00:03:46.263 --> 00:03:52.048
At last, she found her voice and shrieked so loudly that the whole neighborhood heard.

62
00:03:52.049 --> 00:03:57.550
"Sebastian, Sebastian!"

